{
  "suite": "dg14",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "EF.DG14 SecurityInfos parsing: the same SET-of-SEQUENCE walk EF.CardAccess uses, producing typed CA rows and AA rows. Covers CA-only bodies, multi-key DG14s, the pubkey-only body that drives the infer-OID path, keyId-bearing entries, explicit-EC-params and both DH parameter encodings, a PACEInfo sharing the file, AA entries with and without a signature algorithm and alongside CA entries (first-wins ordering material for the AA verifier), the unparseable-SPKI skip (upstream's d2i_PUBKEY nil), and the malformed-entry and version-parse splits at all three version sites. AA-carrying bodies are shared cases. A split pair covers ICAO 9303 P11 App I's PACE-CAM public key, whose SubjectPublicKeyInfo uses the BSI standardizedDomainParameters AlgorithmIdentifier (0.4.0.127.0.7.1.2 plus an INTEGER parameterId) rather than id-ecPublicKey. The Dart parser resolves the parameterId through PACE's own P11 §9.5.1 Table 12 table and yields the key; OpenSSL does not know that OID, so upstream's d2i_PUBKEY nil-returns and SecurityInfo.getInstance skips the entry: a Divergences row, not a bug, since the nil-skip is upstream's documented contract.",
  "runners": [
    "dart",
    "swift"
  ],
  "cases": [
